hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2936","Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Ala’, who said: Sufyan narrated to us, who said: I heard ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informing on the authority of his father, on the authority of ‘A’ishah (RA), who said:\nWe went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She said: “I menstruated, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me while I was weeping. He said: ‘What is the matter with you? Is it your period?’ I said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘This is something that Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam. So do what the pilgrim does, except that you should not perform Tawaf around the House.’”\n\nCHAPTER:"
